Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.76,0:00:22.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,今天的《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:00:21.76,0:00:22.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Today on How It's Made
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.80,0:00:28.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,钉子和订书钉，每天生产2500万枚
Dialogue: 1,0:00:24.80,0:00:28.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Nails and Staples, 25 million produced every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.00,0:00:34.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,护目镜，从刑侦人员到运动员都在用
Dialogue: 1,0:00:30.00,0:00:34.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Safety glasses, from crime scene investigators to sports.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.64,0:00:40.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料，单个纱线筒就能纺出25公里
Dialogue: 1,0:00:36.64,0:00:40.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Fabrics, 25 kilometers from just a single bobbin.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.74,0:00:46.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有自行车，从碳纤维到轻如羽毛的金属合金
Dialogue: 1,0:00:41.74,0:00:46.00,Original,,0,0,0,,And bicycles, from carbon fiber to feather light metal alloys.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.40,0:00:50.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过首先，正如每位手工行家所说
Dialogue: 1,0:00:46.40,0:00:50.40,Original,,0,0,0,,But first, as every DIY expert will tell you,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.56,0:00:55.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,笨工匠怪工具，更笨的则怪钉子
Dialogue: 1,0:00:50.56,0:00:55.68,Original,,0,0,0,,a bad workman blames his tools, and an even worse one blames the nail.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.24,0:00:58.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这下可没有借口了
Dialogue: 1,0:00:56.24,0:00:58.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Well, now there's no excuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.40,0:01:01.74,Translation,,0,0,0,,无论你用砌筑钉、木钉，平头钉还是沉头钉
Dialogue: 1,0:00:58.40,0:01:01.74,Original,,0,0,0,,Whether you're using a masonry, wood, flat head or countersunk
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.74,0:01:06.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,可曾想过这数以百万计的 坚韧小钉子是如何做到分毫不差的
Dialogue: 1,0:01:01.74,0:01:06.80,Original,,0,0,0,,have you ever wondered how they make millions of these tough little pins to exact dimensions?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.64,0:01:16.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,几乎所有钉子都以同样的方式开始它们的旅程
Dialogue: 1,0:01:12.64,0:01:16.32,Original,,0,0,0,,Just about all nails start out their journey in the same way.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.12,0:01:19.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,大多数由高耐久性的碳钢制成
Dialogue: 1,0:01:17.12,0:01:19.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Most are made from highly durable carbon steel.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.16,0:01:22.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们最初以钢丝的形态出现
Dialogue: 1,0:01:20.16,0:01:22.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Which originates in steel wire form.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.64,0:01:29.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,卷在卷筒上，这卷钢丝重达2000多公斤
Dialogue: 1,0:01:24.64,0:01:29.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Rolled up on a drum, this wire weighs in at over 2,000 kilos.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.64,0:01:34.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,钢丝直径6毫米，实在太粗了
Dialogue: 1,0:01:30.64,0:01:34.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The wire's diameter is 6mm, which is too large,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.72,0:01:37.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,因此要通过拉伸工艺减小钢丝直径
Dialogue: 1,0:01:34.72,0:01:37.52,Original,,0,0,0,,so a stretching process reduces the steel's width.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.88,0:01:43.46,Translation,,0,0,0,,经过多个卷筒反复拉伸，钢丝逐渐变细
Dialogue: 1,0:01:38.88,0:01:43.46,Original,,0,0,0,,Using many drums, the wire is pulled repeatedly to gradually thin it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.00,0:01:45.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后钢丝被卷绕到卷筒上
Dialogue: 1,0:01:44.00,0:01:45.60,Original,,0,0,0,,It's then rolled onto a drum.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.84,0:01:59.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,卷满后，这卷钢丝超过23千米，重1136公斤
Dialogue: 1,0:01:51.84,0:01:59.92,Original,,0,0,0,,When full, this roll contains over 23,000 meters of wire, weighing in at 1,136 kilos.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.40,0:02:04.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时钢丝直径已减到2.84毫米
Dialogue: 1,0:02:00.40,0:02:04.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The wire is now a diameter of 2.84mm,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.32,0:02:06.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,还需再减半一次
Dialogue: 1,0:02:04.32,0:02:06.56,Original,,0,0,0,,so will have to be reduced by half again.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.56,0:02:10.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在钢丝被切割成小段
Dialogue: 1,0:02:08.56,0:02:10.48,Original,,0,0,0,,It's now cut into small rods.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.04,0:02:14.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,切割好的钢丝段由这台电磁铁吸起
Dialogue: 1,0:02:11.04,0:02:14.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The cut rods are gathered up with this electromagnet
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.00,0:02:16.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后送入加工它们的机器
Dialogue: 1,0:02:14.00,0:02:16.48,Original,,0,0,0,,and dumped into a machine that will process them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.64,0:02:32.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是重点：钢段由刀片削出钉尖，变成钉子
Dialogue: 1,0:02:26.64,0:02:32.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Now comes the important bit: the rods are turned into nails by a blade that forms the nail's point.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.24,0:02:47.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器用巨大压力压扁钢段末端，制成钉头
Dialogue: 1,0:02:42.24,0:02:47.20,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine forms nail heads by flattening them using great pressure on the rod ends.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.00,0:02:58.62,Translation,,0,0,0,,钉头以每分钟1400个的速度成型
Dialogue: 1,0:02:54.00,0:02:58.62,Original,,0,0,0,,Nail heads are formed at a rate of 1,400 per minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.56,0:03:06.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,钉子的制造到此完成
Dialogue: 1,0:03:04.56,0:03:06.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The manufacturing of the nails is now finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.68,0:03:09.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是包装
Dialogue: 1,0:03:07.68,0:03:09.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Next comes the packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.80,0:03:15.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些钉子嵌在塑料卷条里出售
Dialogue: 1,0:03:12.80,0:03:15.44,Original,,0,0,0,,These nails are sold embedded in plastic rolls.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.96,0:03:24.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器每卷装入167枚钉子
Dialogue: 1,0:03:20.96,0:03:24.80,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine inserts 167 nails into each roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.82,0:03:28.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑料条上有齿，钉子钩在上面
Dialogue: 1,0:03:25.82,0:03:28.96,Original,,0,0,0,,The plastic strip has teeth, and the nails hook into these.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.12,0:03:55.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,制造螺旋钉需要多一道工序
Dialogue: 1,0:03:52.12,0:03:55.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Making spiral nails requires an extra processing step.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.40,0:03:59.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器用这些滚筒给钉子旋出螺旋纹
Dialogue: 1,0:03:56.40,0:03:59.52,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine puts the spiral into the nails with these cylinders.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.00,0:04:02.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,每分钟产出1200枚
Dialogue: 1,0:04:00.00,0:04:02.80,Original,,0,0,0,,and produces 1,200 nails a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.20,0:04:09.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后钉子被拼成条状，供气动射钉枪使用
Dialogue: 1,0:04:05.20,0:04:09.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the nails are put together into strips for use in pneumatic nailing guns.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.56,0:04:20.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,为了固定，钉子上涂覆树脂，4分钟即可干燥
Dialogue: 1,0:04:15.56,0:04:20.64,Original,,0,0,0,,To keep them in place, the nails are coated with the resin that dries in 4 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.96,0:04:27.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是使用条装钉子的射钉装置
Dialogue: 1,0:04:24.96,0:04:27.92,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the nailing device that uses nails on a strip.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.72,0:04:31.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,只需扣动扳机就能把钉子射出
Dialogue: 1,0:04:28.72,0:04:31.12,Original,,0,0,0,,It strikes the nails with just the pull of a trigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.00,0:04:41.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂还生产订书钉
Dialogue: 1,0:04:40.00,0:04:41.68,Original,,0,0,0,,This factory also produces staples.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.88,0:04:45.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,订书钉压制机将80根铁丝压合在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:04:42.88,0:04:45.52,Original,,0,0,0,,The staple press binds 80 iron wires,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.52,0:04:48.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些铁丝已排列整齐、并排摆放
Dialogue: 1,0:04:45.52,0:04:48.24,Original,,0,0,0,,which have been lined up and placed side by side.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.20,0:04:58.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后铁丝被粘合在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:04:57.20,0:04:58.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The wires are then glued together.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.04,0:05:05.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,铁丝最终成为一整条粘连的带条
Dialogue: 1,0:05:03.04,0:05:05.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The wires then come out in one adhered strip.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.32,0:05:10.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,订书钉带条送入这台机器
Dialogue: 1,0:05:08.32,0:05:10.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The staple strips are fed into this machine,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.20,0:05:14.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,它把订书钉切割成所需长度并折弯
Dialogue: 1,0:05:11.20,0:05:14.40,Original,,0,0,0,,which cuts the staples to the desired length and folds
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.40,0:05:18.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,压机使用40顿压力， 一次冲压完成折弯
Dialogue: 1,0:05:14.40,0:05:18.80,Original,,0,0,0,,them in one stroke of this press, applying 40 tons of pressure.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.24,0:05:24.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,订书钉在这台模具上成型
Dialogue: 1,0:05:22.24,0:05:24.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Staples are formed on this gauge,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.48,0:05:27.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,订书钉带条随即进入包装环节
Dialogue: 1,0:05:24.48,0:05:27.20,Original,,0,0,0,,and the staple strips are then ready for packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.68,0:05:35.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂每天总计生产2500万枚钉子和订书钉
Dialogue: 1,0:05:29.68,0:05:35.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Every day, this factory produces a total of 25 million nails and staples.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.20,0:05:46.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们挽救过许多工人和金属工匠的视力
Dialogue: 1,0:05:43.20,0:05:46.48,Original,,0,0,0,,They've saved the sight of many a workman and metalworker.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.44,0:05:50.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,从壁球运动员到刑侦人员
Dialogue: 1,0:05:47.44,0:05:50.24,Original,,0,0,0,,From squash players to crime scene investigators,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.40,0:05:52.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,全世界都信赖它们来保护我们的视力
Dialogue: 1,0:05:50.40,0:05:52.96,Original,,0,0,0,,they are trusted the world over to save our vision.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.92,0:05:56.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,无论你周末想做点手工活
Dialogue: 1,0:05:53.92,0:05:56.88,Original,,0,0,0,,So whether you're doing a spot of DIY this weekend or
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.88,0:06:01.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,还是身处危险环境，你都会想看接下来这个环节
Dialogue: 1,0:05:56.88,0:06:01.12,Original,,0,0,0,,working in a dangerous environment, you'll want to catch. This next segment.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.68,0:06:11.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,许多运动和行业都需要佩戴护目镜
Dialogue: 1,0:06:07.68,0:06:11.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Many sports and trades require the wearing of safety glasses.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.00,0:06:16.38,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些眼镜在这样的模具中注塑制成
Dialogue: 1,0:06:12.00,0:06:16.38,Original,,0,0,0,,These glasses are made by shaping plastic in molds such as this.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.32,0:06:24.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,镜片的光学部分经过精密加工，以保证尽可能透明且不发生变形
Dialogue: 1,0:06:18.32,0:06:24.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The optical part of the lens is mirrored in order to be as transparent as possible without being deformed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.80,0:06:31.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,眼镜主要由熔化的树脂制成
Dialogue: 1,0:06:28.80,0:06:31.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The glasses are made by melting the primary material,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.32,0:06:34.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是一种名为聚碳酸酯的塑料树脂
Dialogue: 1,0:06:32.32,0:06:34.72,Original,,0,0,0,,a plastic resin called polycarbonate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.00,0:06:42.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,树脂颗粒被倒入这台机器中
Dialogue: 1,0:06:40.00,0:06:42.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The resin granules are poured into this machine and
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.24,0:06:46.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,在250摄氏度的温度下熔化为液态
Dialogue: 1,0:06:42.24,0:06:46.00,Original,,0,0,0,,becomes liquefied at a temperature of 250 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.96,0:06:50.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,液态塑料在压力下注入模具
Dialogue: 1,0:06:46.96,0:06:50.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The liquid plastic is injected into the mold under pressure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.00,0:06:58.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑料迅速硬化，随后眼镜从模具中取出
Dialogue: 1,0:06:54.00,0:06:58.96,Original,,0,0,0,,The plastic hardens rapidly and the glasses are then removed from the mold.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.64,0:07:04.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,眼镜被手工分离，并进行初步目检
Dialogue: 1,0:07:00.64,0:07:04.72,Original,,0,0,0,,The glasses are separated by hand and given an initial visual inspection.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.08,0:07:20.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,护目镜经过清洗，去除杂质，为下一道工序做准备
Dialogue: 1,0:07:16.08,0:07:20.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The goggles are washed to eliminate any impurities and to ready them for the next phase.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.24,0:07:35.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们被送往实验室，接受表面处理涂层
Dialogue: 1,0:07:32.24,0:07:35.76,Original,,0,0,0,,They're taken to the laboratory where they're given a coating of surface treatment.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.04,0:07:43.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后眼镜用清水冲洗
Dialogue: 1,0:07:41.04,0:07:43.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The glasses are then rinsed in clear water.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.52,0:07:50.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着眼镜被缓缓浸入化学溶液中
Dialogue: 1,0:07:47.52,0:07:50.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The glasses are then gently soaked in a chemical solution
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.64,0:07:53.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种溶液能防止镜片起雾和刮伤
Dialogue: 1,0:07:50.64,0:07:53.04,Original,,0,0,0,,which prevents misting and scratching of the lens.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.92,0:08:04.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,涂层现在需要进行固化
Dialogue: 1,0:08:01.92,0:08:04.00,Original,,0,0,0,,This coating now has to be cooked.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.56,0:08:08.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,眼镜穿过加热到120摄氏度的烘箱
Dialogue: 1,0:08:04.56,0:08:08.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The glasses are passed through an oven heated to 120 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.76,0:08:13.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,浸泡和固化过程长达2小时
Dialogue: 1,0:08:09.76,0:08:13.12,Original,,0,0,0,,The soaking and cooking process can last up to 2 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.84,0:08:23.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,每副眼镜都要接受检查，以确保镜片上没有瑕疵或变形
Dialogue: 1,0:08:17.84,0:08:23.60,Original,,0,0,0,,Each pair of glasses is inspected to make sure there are no imperfections or distortions in the lenses.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.84,0:08:32.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,眼镜被固定在支架上，便于车床加工
Dialogue: 1,0:08:27.84,0:08:32.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The glasses are placed on a support, securing it for the lathes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.32,0:08:40.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台铣床自动去除最后一块聚碳酸酯
Dialogue: 1,0:08:36.32,0:08:40.00,Original,,0,0,0,,This milling machine automatically removes the last piece of polycarbonate.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.80,0:08:45.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这块料留下是为了让眼镜能够被拿起而无需触碰镜片
Dialogue: 1,0:08:40.80,0:08:45.60,Original,,0,0,0,,which was left in place so that the glasses could be handled without having to touch the lenses.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.00,0:08:51.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后粘上鼻托
Dialogue: 1,0:08:50.00,0:08:51.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The nose piece is then glued on.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.28,0:09:06.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,每批产品中都会抽取几副眼镜进行测试
Dialogue: 1,0:09:03.28,0:09:06.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Certain pairs of glasses are selected from each production run.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.20,0:09:14.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,在这里，他们测试眼镜能否抵挡以140公里时速的撞击的壁球
Dialogue: 1,0:09:07.20,0:09:14.08,Original,,0,0,0,,Here, they evaluate the resistance of the glasses to a squash ball shot at them at 140 kilometers per hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.92,0:09:20.78,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里还用100公里时速的冰球测试曲棍球面罩
Dialogue: 1,0:09:15.92,0:09:20.78,Original,,0,0,0,,Here, a hockey visor is tested against a puck traveling at 100 kilometers per hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.44,0:09:25.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,为符合安全标准，眼镜必须通过这些测试
Dialogue: 1,0:09:21.44,0:09:25.36,Original,,0,0,0,,To conform to safety standards, the glasses must withstand these tests.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.00,0:09:28.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,证明它们确实安全可靠
Dialogue: 1,0:09:26.00,0:09:28.24,Original,,0,0,0,,It confirms that they're truly safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.80,0:09:35.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来进入护目镜的最后组装工序
Dialogue: 1,0:09:32.80,0:09:35.92,Original,,0,0,0,,They now proceed to final assembly steps in making the glasses.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.48,0:09:40.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后几个部件，如塑料镜腿，被安装上去
Dialogue: 1,0:09:36.48,0:09:40.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The last few pieces, such as the plastic ear stems, are installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.80,0:09:51.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,组装完成后，眼镜被装入包装盒
Dialogue: 1,0:09:48.80,0:09:51.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Now completed, the glasses are placed in cases,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.84,0:09:54.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是制造过程的最后一步
Dialogue: 1,0:09:51.84,0:09:54.00,Original,,0,0,0,,and is the final step in their fabrication.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.92,0:10:04.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家公司生产多种护目镜：
Dialogue: 1,0:10:01.92,0:10:04.64,Original,,0,0,0,,This company makes several types of safety glasses:
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.20,0:10:07.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,工业用、曲棍球和橄榄球面罩
Dialogue: 1,0:10:05.20,0:10:07.84,Original,,0,0,0,,industrial, hockey and football visors,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.32,0:10:10.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,以及游泳镜和壁球眼镜
Dialogue: 1,0:10:08.32,0:10:10.72,Original,,0,0,0,,swimming goggles, and squash glasses.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.16,0:10:21.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂每天生产数千副护目镜
Dialogue: 1,0:10:18.16,0:10:21.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The facility turns out thousands of safety glasses
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.28,0:10:26.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,制造这些护目镜所用的聚碳酸酯树脂
Dialogue: 1,0:10:21.28,0:10:26.00,Original,,0,0,0,,every day, and the polycarbonate resin used to make these safety
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.00,0:10:29.26,Translation,,0,0,0,,有朝一日或许能保住你的视力
Dialogue: 1,0:10:26.00,0:10:29.26,Original,,0,0,0,,glasses could one day save your sight.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.80,0:10:34.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来请看《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:10:32.80,0:10:34.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming up on how it's made
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.80,0:10:36.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料
Dialogue: 1,0:10:35.80,0:10:36.32,Original,,0,0,0,,fabrics.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.96,0:10:39.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,工业革命让布料走进千家万户
Dialogue: 1,0:10:36.96,0:10:39.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The Industrial Revolution brought fabric to the masses.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.00,0:10:43.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今，单个纱线筒就能纺出25公里长的布
Dialogue: 1,0:10:40.00,0:10:43.92,Original,,0,0,0,,And today, a single bobbin can produce 25 kilometers of cloth.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.88,0:10:48.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,自行车：配备多级变速和高科技材料
Dialogue: 1,0:10:44.88,0:10:48.40,Original,,0,0,0,,And bicycles, with multiple gears and high-tech materials,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.40,0:10:52.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,无论幽静小路还是最崎岖的山地都如履平地
Dialogue: 1,0:10:48.40,0:10:52.96,Original,,0,0,0,,they're made to tackle everything from quiet paths to the most rugged mountain trails.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.92,0:10:55.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍作休息，马上回来
Dialogue: 1,0:10:53.92,0:10:55.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Join us after the break.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.80,0:11:06.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎回到《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:11:04.80,0:11:06.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to How It's Made.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.68,0:11:12.14,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后，我们将看自行车， 从多级变速到高科技材料
Dialogue: 1,0:11:07.68,0:11:12.14,Original,,0,0,0,,Later, we look at bikes from multiple gears to high-tech materials
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.14,0:11:15.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,从平顺的公路到崎岖的山地
Dialogue: 1,0:11:12.14,0:11:15.36,Original,,0,0,0,,from quiet cycle paths to the most rugged mountain trails.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.28,0:11:23.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,不过首先，远古人类靠兽皮来抵御风雨
Dialogue: 1,0:11:17.28,0:11:23.68,Original,,0,0,0,,But first, early man relied on animal skins to protect himself against the elements.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.32,0:11:27.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,后来，布料让人类不再需要为穿衣而捕猎
Dialogue: 1,0:11:24.32,0:11:27.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Eventually, fabrics eliminated the need to hunt for our clothes,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.56,0:11:31.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,织布机的发明让布料走进千家万户
Dialogue: 1,0:11:28.56,0:11:31.84,Original,,0,0,0,,and the invention of the loom brought cloth to the masses.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.72,0:11:36.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今，纺织厂能织出各种图案和颜色的布料
Dialogue: 1,0:11:32.72,0:11:36.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Today, textile mills make fabrics in every conceivable pattern and color.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.26,0:11:43.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料由成千上万根交织的纱线织成
Dialogue: 1,0:11:40.26,0:11:43.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Fabric is made from thousands of braided threads.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.84,0:11:46.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂有700个涤纶纱线筒
Dialogue: 1,0:11:43.84,0:11:46.40,Original,,0,0,0,,This mill has 700 bobbins of polyester,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.72,0:11:50.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个纱线筒装有25万米纱线
Dialogue: 1,0:11:46.72,0:11:50.80,Original,,0,0,0,,with each bobbin containing 250,000 meters of thread.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.44,0:12:00.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这个装置称为经纱装置，汇集700根纤维
Dialogue: 1,0:11:55.44,0:12:00.00,Original,,0,0,0,,This unit, called a warp, takes the 700 fibers, assembles.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.24,0:12:02.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,再将其梳理成分开的纱束
Dialogue: 1,0:12:00.24,0:12:02.16,Original,,0,0,0,,Then combs them into separate strands.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.52,0:12:10.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,再不断加入其他纱线，最终共有7000根排列整齐的纱线
Dialogue: 1,0:12:05.52,0:12:10.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Other strands are added until, in total, there are 7,000 aligned threads.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.80,0:12:16.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料由互相成90度交织的纱线组成
Dialogue: 1,0:12:12.80,0:12:16.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The fabric is composed of threads braided at 90 degrees to each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.52,0:12:19.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,经纱沿纵向排列
Dialogue: 1,0:12:17.52,0:12:19.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the warp threads are assembled lengthwise,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.16,0:12:21.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,其他纱线则横向穿过
Dialogue: 1,0:12:20.16,0:12:21.84,Original,,0,0,0,,whilst others are joined diagonally.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.84,0:12:27.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,为防止纱线断裂，它们要先涂一层胶水
Dialogue: 1,0:12:23.84,0:12:27.36,Original,,0,0,0,,To prevent the threads from tearing, they pass through a bin of glue.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.24,0:12:30.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些滚筒去除多余的胶水
Dialogue: 1,0:12:28.24,0:12:30.00,Original,,0,0,0,,These rollers eliminate the surplus.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.88,0:12:34.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,染色前胶水会被水洗去
Dialogue: 1,0:12:30.88,0:12:34.00,Original,,0,0,0,,The glue will be removed with water before dyeing the threads.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.32,0:12:43.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些大型绿色滚筒加热并烘干纱线上的胶水
Dialogue: 1,0:12:40.32,0:12:43.20,Original,,0,0,0,,These large green cylinders are heated and dry the glue on the threads.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.40,0:12:48.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,粘合好的纱束在织机滚筒上被分开
Dialogue: 1,0:12:46.40,0:12:48.96,Original,,0,0,0,,The glued strands are separated on this loom roller.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.52,0:13:03.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,每根纱线都要穿过综丝，以织出特定花纹
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.52,0:13:03.28,Annotation,,0,0,0,,综丝: 中间有一个小孔，叫做综眼。每根综丝控制一根经纱。织布时，综丝上下移动，带动经纱分开，好让纬纱穿过去。
Dialogue: 1,0:12:59.52,0:13:03.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Each thread must pass through a blade to produce a specific design.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.16,0:13:07.22,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台设备将7000根纱线
Dialogue: 1,0:13:04.16,0:13:07.22,Original,,0,0,0,,This piece of equipment takes the 7,000 strands of thread
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.22,0:13:11.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,逐一穿过综丝，操作极其精确
Dialogue: 1,0:13:07.22,0:13:11.52,Original,,0,0,0,,one by one and passes them through the blade in a highly precise operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.16,0:13:25.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,就这样，织布终于开始了
Dialogue: 1,0:13:23.16,0:13:25.44,Original,,0,0,0,,And so the weaving finally begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.64,0:13:30.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,在织机滚筒上，经纱由气流喷入
Dialogue: 1,0:13:26.64,0:13:30.56,Original,,0,0,0,,On this loom roller, the warp thread is inserted by a jet of air.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.76,0:13:40.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,织布机将两个各有7000根纱线的织机滚筒合在一起
Dialogue: 1,0:13:35.76,0:13:40.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The weaving machine assembles two loom rollers made of 7,000 strands.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.40,0:13:45.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,布幅宽达3.65米
Dialogue: 1,0:13:42.40,0:13:45.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The fabric reaches a width of 3.65 meters.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.00,0:13:49.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,深色纱线被织入布料中
Dialogue: 1,0:13:45.76,0:13:49.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The dark threads are inserted into the weave.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.76,0:13:55.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,综丝取出一组纱线，以便织入下一组
Dialogue: 1,0:13:51.76,0:13:55.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The blades remove one set of strands to insert the next ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.72,0:14:03.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料实现了工业化生产
Dialogue: 1,0:14:00.72,0:14:03.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The fabric is made on an industrial scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.16,0:14:08.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,这个纱线筒竟装有250公里长的纱线
Dialogue: 1,0:14:04.16,0:14:08.48,Original,,0,0,0,,This bobbin contains an amazing 250 kilometers of thread.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.72,0:14:22.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,织布机满负荷运转时，每分钟完成600次纱线交织
Dialogue: 1,0:14:16.72,0:14:22.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Operating at full tilt, the loom makes 600 thread intersections every minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.16,0:14:39.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,织布工序完成，接下来进入下一道工序
Dialogue: 1,0:14:36.16,0:14:39.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Weaving is now over, and we move onto the next step.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.24,0:14:41.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,水洗和染色
Dialogue: 1,0:14:40.24,0:14:41.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Washing and dyeing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.04,0:14:46.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,在80摄氏度的皂液中
Dialogue: 1,0:14:43.04,0:14:46.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Washing is done in a soapy solution at 80 degrees in a
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.72,0:14:50.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,以每分钟60米的速度连续水洗
Dialogue: 1,0:14:46.72,0:14:50.24,Original,,0,0,0,,continuous manner at a speed of 60 meters of fabric per minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.08,0:14:55.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料再放入30摄氏度的清水中漂洗
Dialogue: 1,0:14:52.08,0:14:55.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The fabric is rinsed in clear water at 30 degrees.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.20,0:14:58.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是染色
Dialogue: 1,0:14:57.20,0:14:58.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Next, it's onto dyeing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.52,0:15:00.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是通过喷射染色机完成的
Dialogue: 1,0:14:59.52,0:15:00.80,Original,,0,0,0,,This is done with jets.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.60,0:15:06.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,将长达12000米的布料放入加入染料的清水中
Dialogue: 1,0:15:01.60,0:15:06.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Up to 12,000 meters of fabric are placed in clean water into which colorants are added.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.76,0:15:11.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料在加热的染液中， 浸泡约6小时
Dialogue: 1,0:15:07.76,0:15:11.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The solution is heated, and the fabric soaks here for about 6 hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.04,0:15:15.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后用温水漂洗
Dialogue: 1,0:15:13.04,0:15:15.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Then it will be rinsed in lukewarm water.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.98,0:15:25.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料随后放入料仓
Dialogue: 1,0:15:23.98,0:15:25.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The fabric is then placed in a bin.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.20,0:15:28.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器称为开幅机
Dialogue: 1,0:15:27.20,0:15:28.80,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine is called an opener.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.36,0:15:33.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,它展开并抻平布料，再卷绕到巨大的滚筒上
Dialogue: 1,0:15:29.36,0:15:33.92,Original,,0,0,0,,It unfolds and stretches the material before rolling it up on an immense roller.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.94,0:15:42.74,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在，这卷布快卷满了
Dialogue: 1,0:15:39.94,0:15:42.74,Original,,0,0,0,,And now, the roll is almost full.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.04,0:15:47.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后一道工序是热定型
Dialogue: 1,0:15:45.04,0:15:47.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The final step is thermo-setting,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.76,0:15:50.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,高温烘箱将布料烘干
Dialogue: 1,0:15:47.76,0:15:50.08,Original,,0,0,0,,where a high-temperature oven dries the fabric.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.54,0:15:54.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,温度高达200摄氏度
Dialogue: 1,0:15:51.54,0:15:54.72,Original,,0,0,0,,At temperatures reaching 200 degrees centigrade,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.72,0:15:56.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,布料在其中运行45秒
Dialogue: 1,0:15:54.72,0:15:56.96,Original,,0,0,0,,the fabric circulates for 45 seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.72,0:16:02.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,每一卷成品布都重达1500公斤
Dialogue: 1,0:15:58.72,0:16:02.88,Original,,0,0,0,,With each finished roll weighing in at a hefty 1,500 kilos,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.60,0:16:06.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,装有25公里长的布料
Dialogue: 1,0:16:03.60,0:16:06.56,Original,,0,0,0,,they hold 25 kilometers of fabric.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.00,0:16:17.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,自行车早已不同于最初的设计
Dialogue: 1,0:16:14.00,0:16:17.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Bicycles have come a long way from the original design.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.64,0:16:20.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,如今它们配备多级变速
Dialogue: 1,0:16:18.64,0:16:20.56,Original,,0,0,0,,They now feature multiple gears,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.96,0:16:25.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,以及碳纤维车架、轻如羽毛的金属合金等高科技材料
Dialogue: 1,0:16:20.96,0:16:25.68,Original,,0,0,0,,high-tech materials like carbon fiber frames, and feather-light metal alloys.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.40,0:16:28.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,它们无论面对安静的自行车道
Dialogue: 1,0:16:26.40,0:16:28.72,Original,,0,0,0,,And they're made to tackle everything from quiet bike
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.72,0:16:31.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,还是最崎岖的山地都应付自如
Dialogue: 1,0:16:28.72,0:16:31.36,Original,,0,0,0,,paths to the most rugged mountain trails.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.72,0:16:46.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,1790年法国的发明，最早的自行车形似双轮木马，没有踏板和车把
Dialogue: 1,0:16:38.72,0:16:46.72,Original,,0,0,0,,A French invention of 1790, the first bicycle resembled a two-wheeled wooden horse without pedals or handlebars.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.28,0:16:51.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,1817年，一位德国人给它加上了方向控制
Dialogue: 1,0:16:47.28,0:16:51.04,Original,,0,0,0,,In 1817, a German gave it direction control.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.68,0:16:55.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,1861年，法国人又在前轮上加装了踏板
Dialogue: 1,0:16:51.68,0:16:55.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The addition of pedals to the front wheels came from France in 1861.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.56,0:17:00.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,1870年，英国人加上了硕大的前轮
Dialogue: 1,0:16:56.56,0:17:00.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The large front wheel was added by the British in 1870.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.68,0:17:05.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,到1903年，著名的环法自行车赛开赛
Dialogue: 1,0:17:01.68,0:17:05.36,Original,,0,0,0,,And by 1903, the famed Tour de France began.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.92,0:17:20.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,自行车是一件精美的机械杰作
Dialogue: 1,0:17:17.92,0:17:20.64,Original,,0,0,0,,A bicycle is a beautiful piece of engineering.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.76,0:17:24.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,车架由钢或铬钼钢制成
Dialogue: 1,0:17:21.76,0:17:24.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The frames are made of steel or chromoly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.72,0:17:28.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,制造从这些中空钢管开始
Dialogue: 1,0:17:26.72,0:17:28.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Fabrication begins with these hollow tubes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.92,0:17:33.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,切管机将钢管切断，再送往弯管机
Dialogue: 1,0:17:29.92,0:17:33.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The tube cutter slices the steel before sending it to the bender.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.04,0:17:37.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,弯管机对钢管进行冷弯
Dialogue: 1,0:17:35.04,0:17:37.12,Original,,0,0,0,,The bender curves the tubes cold,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.44,0:17:40.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,以强大压力压向弯管模具
Dialogue: 1,0:17:37.44,0:17:40.24,Original,,0,0,0,,exerting strong pressure against the bending jig.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.40,0:17:49.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,钢管接下来要进行加工，按长度切割
Dialogue: 1,0:17:46.40,0:17:49.68,Original,,0,0,0,,The tubes must now be machined and are cut into lengths
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.08,0:17:52.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,以便彼此正确套接
Dialogue: 1,0:17:50.08,0:17:52.40,Original,,0,0,0,,so they can correctly fit into one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.44,0:17:56.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,加工过程中，润滑液为钢管降温
Dialogue: 1,0:17:53.44,0:17:56.32,Original,,0,0,0,,During this operation, lubricants cool the tube.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.86,0:18:02.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,切割时会考虑其他部件的插接角度
Dialogue: 1,0:17:57.86,0:18:02.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The tube is cut, taking into consideration the insertion angle of the other pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.76,0:18:06.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,需要焊接在一起的钢管被放入这个支架
Dialogue: 1,0:18:03.76,0:18:06.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Tubes to be welded together are placed in this support.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.64,0:18:14.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,加入银和青铜以增强强度、提高焊接质量
Dialogue: 1,0:18:10.64,0:18:14.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Silver and bronze is added to increase strength and produce a better weld.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.84,0:18:29.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,车架焊接约需2分钟，温度高达800摄氏度
Dialogue: 1,0:18:23.84,0:18:29.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Welding of the frame requires about 2 minutes at a temperature of 800 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.32,0:18:37.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,焊好后，部件需4分钟冷却
Dialogue: 1,0:18:34.32,0:18:37.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Once welded, the part takes 4 minutes to cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.08,0:18:41.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,构成自行车的其余钢管也已加工完成
Dialogue: 1,0:18:38.08,0:18:41.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The rest of the tubes that go to make up the bike are completed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.24,0:18:51.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时必须校正车架，因为焊接时车架可能发生变形
Dialogue: 1,0:18:46.24,0:18:51.12,Original,,0,0,0,,At this stage, it's important to straighten the frame which may have deformed during welding.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.00,0:18:54.14,Translation,,0,0,0,,检查各钢管的对位情况
Dialogue: 1,0:18:52.00,0:18:54.14,Original,,0,0,0,,The alignment of the tubes are verified
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.14,0:18:58.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后用工具进行冷校直，使其尺寸准确
Dialogue: 1,0:18:54.14,0:18:58.72,Original,,0,0,0,,and then straightened out cold with a tool that sets it to the right dimensions.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.52,0:19:04.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是喷漆工序
Dialogue: 1,0:19:03.52,0:19:04.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Next comes the paint job.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.68,0:19:09.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,用喷枪喷漆，漆料借助静电吸附在车架上
Dialogue: 1,0:19:05.68,0:19:09.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Paint is applied with a spray gun and adheres to the frame by static contact.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.72,0:19:16.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后漆面在天然气烘箱中以218摄氏度烘烤15分钟
Dialogue: 1,0:19:10.72,0:19:16.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the paint will be baked in a natural gas oven at 218 degrees for 15 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.56,0:19:23.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,车架冷却后即可开始组装
Dialogue: 1,0:19:20.56,0:19:23.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The frame is now cooled and the assembly can begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.38,0:19:30.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,贴上品牌标牌
Dialogue: 1,0:19:29.38,0:19:30.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The labels are applied.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.36,0:19:34.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,在工厂另一区域，车把正在组装
Dialogue: 1,0:19:31.36,0:19:34.40,Original,,0,0,0,,In a different part of the factory, the handlebars are assembled.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.60,0:19:38.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,刹车和变速机构被安装上去
Dialogue: 1,0:19:35.60,0:19:38.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The mechanism for the brakes and the gears are installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.04,0:19:50.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来是轮圈
Dialogue: 1,0:19:49.04,0:19:50.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Next comes the wheel rims.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.36,0:19:56.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个铝制车轮的36根不锈钢辐条均由手工安装
Dialogue: 1,0:19:51.36,0:19:56.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The 36 stainless steel spokes of each aluminium wheel are installed manually.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.68,0:20:03.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些工人的巧手让他们每小时能为65个轮圈装上辐条
Dialogue: 1,0:19:57.68,0:20:03.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The dexterity of these workers allows them to install spokes on 65 wheel rims every hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.80,0:20:07.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这把辐条工具让他们能把辐条旋入轮圈
Dialogue: 1,0:20:04.80,0:20:07.92,Original,,0,0,0,,This spoke tool allows them to screw the spokes into the rim.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.20,0:20:19.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器对辐条施加压力，以达到所需的张紧度
Dialogue: 1,0:20:15.20,0:20:19.76,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine exerts a pressure on the spokes in order to achieve the desired tension.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.48,0:20:23.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,张力过大或不足，轮圈都会变形
Dialogue: 1,0:20:20.48,0:20:23.84,Original,,0,0,0,,If there is too much or not enough tension, the rim will be crooked.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.84,0:20:33.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器负责校正轮圈
Dialogue: 1,0:20:31.84,0:20:33.44,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine aligns the rims.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.08,0:20:38.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,它自动调节辐条，使车轮完全笔直
Dialogue: 1,0:20:34.08,0:20:38.08,Original,,0,0,0,,It automatically adjusts the spokes so that the wheel will be truly straight.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.76,0:20:45.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来把内胎和外胎装到轮圈上
Dialogue: 1,0:20:41.76,0:20:45.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Now for the placing of the inner tubes and the tires on the wheel rims.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.16,0:20:56.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,自行车被倒置，从一个车间传送到另一个车间
Dialogue: 1,0:20:52.16,0:20:56.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Set upside down, the bicycle circulates from one workshop to another,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.80,0:20:58.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,在这里安装最后的机械部件：
Dialogue: 1,0:20:56.80,0:20:58.96,Original,,0,0,0,,where they will install the last mechanical parts:
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.08,0:21:05.38,Translation,,0,0,0,,车把、脚踏、前叉、刹车以及链条机构，全部由手工安装
Dialogue: 1,0:21:00.08,0:21:05.38,Original,,0,0,0,,the handlebars, pedals, forks, brakes, and chain mechanisms are all installed manually.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.08,0:21:11.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这里他们旋上后刹车座
Dialogue: 1,0:21:10.08,0:21:11.92,Original,,0,0,0,,Here they screw on the rear brake plate.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.08,0:21:21.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后，他们检查每一辆自行车，确保螺栓
Dialogue: 1,0:21:18.08,0:21:21.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Finally, they inspect each bicycle to make sure that the bolts
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.84,0:21:24.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,拧紧到位，各部件运转正常
Dialogue: 1,0:21:21.84,0:21:24.32,Original,,0,0,0,,are well tightened and that everything's working properly.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.04,0:21:26.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后进入包装环节
Dialogue: 1,0:21:25.04,0:21:26.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Then, it's onto packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.60,0:21:33.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂每天生产2500辆自行车
Dialogue: 1,0:21:29.60,0:21:33.60,Original,,0,0,0,,This factory makes 2,500 bicycles every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.40,0:21:40.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,每辆重11.4公斤，可骑行数千公里
Dialogue: 1,0:21:34.40,0:21:40.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Each one weighs 11.4 kilos and will run for thousands of kilometers.
